extends RefCounted
## Section data (package P10): the data contracts (NPC roster, race perks, game balance), the hardened LuaRuntime (parser,
## semantics, load-time lint, generic kinds loader, passthrough of shop / recipe fields), the late-bound helpers of
## scripts/data (Svc, LuaData, SaveCodec, ItemKinds) and the tools/lua tooling.
##
## Named checks (plan R.2 / addendum 4.4): data.lua_probes, data.lint_clean, data.kinds_shops_recipes,
## data.content_flag_identifiers, data.kinds_shops_recipes_passthrough, data.svc_static_call_fallbacks,
## data.roster_has_feature_npcs, plus data.config_documented_keys, data.roster_fields, data.race_perks_complete,
## data.crops_complete, data.numbers_positive, data.lint_rules, data.parser_*, data.semantics_* ...
##
## Fixtures: tests/fixtures/lua/*.lua. The 23 audit probes and their REAL Lua 5.4 reference values
## (tests/fixtures/lua/probe_expected.json, regenerated by tools/lua/gen_probe_ref.sh) are replayed through the runtime.
## Cross-package subjects that land later (dialogue files of P14 / V7, shops of P12/F1, the quest files of F1 / DR7 / N04) are
## reported as SKIP until they exist; the contract (ids, shape) is asserted from day one.
##
## v2 (package V1-cast-data + amendments RT20, AG1): 22 citizens of the v2 cast (15 + 7) and the eight citizens of the towns track (30 rows,
## `routine = true` on all of them), four races (animal fairy hobbit ghost), two heroes per race, the eight ghost perk keys. The roster pins read IDS
## and FIELDS, never a row count: a data-only citizen is green (roster_accepts_data_only_citizen). The vocabularies of the rows (areas, roles,
## schedules, ages) come from the data (lua/config/npcs.lua `npc_vocab`); the constants below are their contract floor.
## Named checks of this change: data.roster_ids, roster_fields, roster_30_rows_valid, roster_accepts_data_only_citizen, race_perks_complete,
## race_skins_match_characters.
